  "revision_note": "20261105 (candidate-disposition-20261105): candidate disposition (design 2026-10-12 item 3, author 2026-11-05). When the last member_cohort lists candidates the final answer carries task_scope {recommendations_requested, statement} and non_recommendations [{member_id, reason_code, evidence_ids, explanation}]; when recommendations are requested every candidate on the page has a recommendation or a supported non-recommendation, otherwise validation fails (CANDIDATE_NOT_DISPOSED) and the answer is incomplete. Empty cohorts keep the previous contract. Only w05/integration.py and w05/semantics.py change, plus tests; customer functions, YAML, data, metrics and cohort results unchanged. 20261106 (disposition-tolerance-20261106, fde-sandbox c9e3123b): author 2026-11-06 merged W05～W08 plan items 1, 2, 4. When recommendations are not requested, non_recommendations stays empty (prompt and schema description); with nobody to dispose of, task_scope / empty non_recommendations / empty set fields no longer fail the format; an answer that fails validation shows the program fixed summary (or one fixed sentence), the model text stays in model_claim. Only w05/integration.py and its test change; customer functions, YAML, data, metrics and cohort results unchanged. 20261106 (failed-summary-wording-20261106, fde-sandbox 95590d98): the fixed sentence shown when an answer fails validation and the contract has no fixed summary is reworded for business readers (author 2026-11-06). One string in w05/integration.py; nothing else changes. 20261106 (failed-summary-hook-fix-20261106): packaging fix. The weekly package has no final_schema hook (mainline adds it for W08), so the two failed_summary calls use the module function final_contract, as the surrounding validate() calls already do. Without this, an answer that failed validation raised AttributeError. Behaviour otherwise as failed-summary-wording-20261106. 20261109 (dimension-resolution-20261109, fde-sandbox d3101f6f; formal cohort W03 grading, author 11-09): the dimension check judges every group-by with the name MetricFlow itself resolves for the query (explain of the same request the engine sends); list_group_bys lists an entity reached through a join (home_store owned by members, for an order metric) without its path, so it was judged queryable as home_store and the query failed (NATIVE_QUERY_FAILED); now per_metric maps it to member__home_store (an entity not accepted as is is tried behind each entity of the metric, kept only when exactly one spelling resolves). A loaded project keeps its dimensions.json until it is loaded again. candidate_only.json published_to is relative to the project root (else ..), no machine path. platform/fde_product/metrics/validation.py and builder.py only; data, metrics, prompts unchanged."
